Z||000000||theogre||07-16-2001||09:06 PM||||I've updated the coolant filling page. It now includes how to fill after flushing to get a 50/50 mix with the least amount of headache. I just assumed people would figure that out but according to the IMCool article linked in that page even many profesional techs don't do it right so I added it. <P>I've added an expanded page on brake fluid to the cave. This new page should better explain the diferant fluid types. (I finally found data on the DOT 5.1 stuff...)<P>In the brake service article there is now a side page with a color cutaway of the original style rear caliper.<P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||10
Z||000001||StuGood||07-17-2001||01:48 PM||||Ogre, thanks for the updates - your cave is one of the best sources for Fiero info.  Especially appreciate the cutaway of the rear caliper - makes it so even a dumb engineer can understand it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Normally when I have caliper problems, I just install a rebuilt, but I also like to know what's going on in there.  Now I know what the "2-way check valve" in the end of the piston is trying to do, and why there shouldn't be any fluid in there.    <P>Haven't messed with the brakes on my 1988 Fiero, but they definitely need attention.  It'll be awhile before I get to that.  Too bad core charges on the calipers are so high - at least the 1984-87's.  It'd be hard to <B>not</B> turn one in, and keep one for cutaway photos, etc.||||reg||14
